Finding: {"title":"Lead-bonus PATCH allows any authenticated user to self-verify their own instructor bonus with no admin gate","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"Instructor compensation integrity","files":["src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:5238-5288"],"detail":"PATCH /locations/:locationId/checkride-history/:checkrideId/lead-bonus is gated only by requireAuth() and lets the caller set leadInstructorId, onTime, firstPass, and verified directly. Nothing checks that the caller is an admin, or that the caller is not the leadInstructorId being verified. This contrasts with the rest of the file's careful isTenantAdmin()/requireAdmin() gating on financially meaningful fields (examiner email, packet template admin actions, etc.).","impact":"An instructor could set their own lead-bonus record's verified: true (self-attesting eligibility for a bonus) without any admin review, if the UI surfaces this control to non-admin instructor accounts. No downstream payroll automation was found consuming this field in the current codebase, which limits the immediate blast radius, but the field's name and shape strongly suggest compensation intent.","recommendation":"Gate `verified` (and ideally the whole endpoint) behind requireAdmin(), or at minimum reject a request where the acting user's id equals leadInstructorId.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

